  "text": "The Moon is our closest neighbour in space. It is not a star, and it has no light of its own. We see it because the sun shines on it. The Moon is very far away, but it moves around our planet in about one month.\n\nThe Moon has no air and no water, so nothing lives there. Its surface is grey and full of big holes. These holes are called craters. On the Moon, you feel much lighter, and you can jump very high!",
